stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> IDLE
    IDLE --> RA_MSG1: strongest cell >= -115 dBm<br/>(after 1 s search if a failure occurred)
    state "Random Access (RACH)" as RA {
        RA_MSG1 --> RA_MSG2: RAR received<br/>(timing advance)
        RA_MSG1 --> RA_MSG1: no RAR<br/>(power ramp, retry)
        RA_MSG2 --> RA_MSG3: UL grant + TA applied
        RA_MSG3 --> RA_MSG4: RRC connection<br/>request sent
        RA_MSG4 --> RA_MSG1: preamble collision<br/>(random back-off)
    }
    RA_MSG4 --> CONNECTED: contention resolved
    RA_MSG1 --> IDLE: attempts exhausted<br/>(RACH failure)
    CONNECTED --> HANDOVER: policy fires<br/>(naive or hysteresis + TTT)
    HANDOVER --> CONNECTED: access at target done<br/>(serving := target)
    HANDOVER --> IDLE: HO failure<br/>(command lost / target too weak)
    CONNECTED --> IDLE: RLF: serving < -110 dBm<br/>for 500 ms (too late)
